From b87e1cbcbc5e1a83fa128a8d4aef77040ee5acdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 10:39:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0110 -- AdLib OPL2 SDL foundation (PIT/INT8 pump +
 predicate + OPL2)

Campaign 2 (native AdLib / OPL-FM music), Phase 1 SDL side. A pure AdLib /
OPL-only card (incl. a PicoGUS in /mode adlib) has no Sound Blaster, so the
SB16 IRQ-5 that drives the MIDI tick (Lever 2b) never fires -- the music has
no clock. This patch supplies the SB-independent SDL primitives the engine
side (MidiBackendOpl2 + AUDIO_BACKEND=adlib boot-gate, a separate nx step)
will consume. Design + lead decisions: docs/internal/ADLIB-NATIVE-DESIGN.md
sec.3/7 + sec.10.

Why DOS needs this: on a no-SB box the only SDL audio driver (the SB backend)
cannot open, and even if the engine boots silent there is no SB DMA IRQ to
ride for the MIDI clock. The OPL register transport + detect are ALREADY
SB-independent (SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister / SDL_DOSOpl3Detect); the only thing
tying OPL music to the SB is the pump. So Campaign 2 is a pump + chip-init
problem, solved here:

1. PIT/INT8 OPL music pump (new header SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h; impl in
   SDL_dos_audio_synth.c):
   - SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStart(int hz) reprograms 8253 PIT ch0 from the BIOS
     18.2065 Hz to `hz` (engine passes the resolved rate; ~120 recommended),
     hooks IRQ-0 via DOS_HookInterruptReplace (an IRET wrapper; we own the
     EOI), and from that ISR drives the SAME registered MIDI tick callback the
     SB path uses (snapshotted via SDL_DOSMidiTickGetRegistered). The original
     BIOS INT 8 is chained at the divided rate via a fractional accumulator
     (s_bios_accum += div; chain when it rolls 65536) so the BIOS handler fires
     at exactly PIT_INPUT/65536 == 18.2065 Hz regardless of our rate, keeping
     DOS time-of-day correct. The chain uses the canonical DJGPP pushfl+lcall
     idiom to the saved protected-mode vector (which issues its own EOI).
   - SINGLE OWNER of PIT ch0: Start REFUSES if SDL_DOSAudioSB_IsDeviceHot(), so
     the SB-IRQ clock and the PIT clock can never both drive the tick. The pump
     is started only on the no-SB AdLib path; SB-present configs are unchanged.
   - SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStop restores PIT ch0 to divisor 0 (65536 -> 18.2065
     Hz) and unhooks IRQ-0 WITHOUT masking it (a left-reprogrammed PIT makes
     the DOS clock run fast after quit). Idempotent. Must run on teardown +
     atexit (engine wires it).
   - ISR + chain helper + all ISR-touched data are DPMI-locked at Start; the
     ISR does no malloc/FPU/SDL-call (now_ms via a us->ms accumulator loop, no
     in-ISR 64-bit divide).
   - SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpActive() accessor.

2. Shared ISR-active predicate SDL_DOSMidiIsrAnyActive() (SDL_dosmidi_tick.h):
   true if EITHER the SB-IRQ MIDI tick OR the PIT pump is active. The engine's
   MidiScheduler reentrancy guards (MidiIsrCriticalSection cli/sti,
   _refresh_isr_buffer early-return, the OPL backend instance DPMI-lock, the
   runFade per-frame-tick skip) switch to this so they engage under either
   clock -- without it, under the AdLib path the SB-only predicate is false
   while a REAL IRQ-0 ISR reads the scheduler data (a freeze/corruption
   hazard). Required correctness item per lead decision (c).

3. OPL2 chip helpers (SDL_dos_audio_synth.c/.h): SDL_DOSOpl2Detect (reuses the
   OPL3 timer-1 detect), SDL_DOSOpl2InitChip (WSE on, 0xBD cleared, 9 voices
   KEY-OFF; NO 0x105/0x104, NO secondary bank), SDL_DOSOpl2Shutdown (9-voice
   TL=0x3F sweep + KEY-OFF + 0xBD clear). Voices 0-8 are all primary-bank, so
   the existing voice/patch/note helpers serve the OPL2 backend unchanged.

Supporting change: DOS_UnhookInterrupt's `SDL_assert(hook->irq > 0)` relaxed to
`>= 0` so IRQ-0 can be unhooked (callers must pass disable_interrupt=false for
the timer). No other behavior change.

SB-present path is unchanged: the pump is never started when an SB is hot
(belt-and-braces refuse), the OPL3 backend + SB IRQ-5 clock are untouched, and
the new predicate is a superset that returns the same value when only the SB
path is active. Foundation-only: not end-to-end testable until the engine side
(MidiBackendOpl2 + adlib boot-gate); this confirms compile + symbol export.

Deferred (coordination / later phases, per the design + lead decisions): the
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_OPL_TIMER_HZ + OPL2_PORT hints (engine reads HZ and passes it
to Start; the 0x388 port override is a later additive item), smoke BANNERS
entries (Phase 2 -- the banners only emit on the engine-enabled AdLib path), and
docs/BOOT.md rows (nx-engine owns per the design unless reassigned).

g2k-validation item ([[dosbox_not_proxy]]): the IRQ-0 EOI/chain split + the
pushfl+lcall chain to the BIOS INT 8 are the BIOS-tick-correctness risk the
design flagged MEDIUM; they require real-HW confirmation (DOSBox-X cannot
validate IRQ-0 timing). Foundation compiles + exports; the quit-path PIT
restore must be ear/clock-checked on g2k once the engine side lands.

Workspace-local patch; not upstreamed (sdl_ai_policy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
